{"id": "EUVD-2026-59556", "enisaUuid": "b8c986c1-32cf-35c1-b76b-662bc9d54686", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: rtw89: add bounds check on firmware mac_id in link lookup\n\nThe mac_id field in RX descriptors is 8 bits wide (0-255), but\nassoc_link_on_macid[] has only RTW89_MAX_MAC_ID_NUM (128) entries.\nWhile the driver currently assigns mac_id values below 128, the\ndescriptor value comes from firmware and is not validated before use\nas an array index. Add a defensive bounds check in\nrtw89_assoc_link_rcu_dereference() to guard against out-of-range\nfirmware values.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:59:17", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T19:05:43", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ad445de67359f24088d4305c05fbd7e34c4e35e3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/920101305e7601a33b9e01019f4ca526af2526ae", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6d88244bb129755acca696f9227200f4a2d106a6"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-74409", "GHSA-58gw-vjvj-7rmp"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.38, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "03b005c6-9f05-3b87-87c7-39a2d7056470", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "144c6cd24b3556e6e7a14271cee57a42ebf97450 <ad445de67359f24088d4305c05fbd7e34c4e35e3"}, {"id": "095b8bdf-ed17-3870-960c-c03b71c0a07d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "144c6cd24b3556e6e7a14271cee57a42ebf97450 <6d88244bb129755acca696f9227200f4a2d106a6"}, {"id": "31866ebe-a414-3718-bc7a-247735e7aceb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.14"}, {"id": "3afe4c43-e829-32d3-9c46-8d9d37aa69dc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "5b5220c8-2006-35f8-8c7e-b7506d2dab60", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": 